From 98f0329140f272d9919a22d0585cbe488a702548 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 02:15:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/42] Remove the You and Google section from settings

The main settings screen opened with a You and Google section containing a Sign in row and a Google services entry. Neither can function in this build: sign-in requires Google API keys that are not compiled in, and Sync is not part of this build.

Removes both rows and the section header, using the fragment own removePreferenceIfPresent helper - the same mechanism it already uses to hide the sign-in row when shouldShowSignInPref returns false. That removes from the preference screen while the object stays in mAllPreferences, so the earlier SignInPreference.initialize call cannot hit a null.

Verified on device: settings now opens directly to Basics with no empty heading, and no crash.
---
 .../chrome/browser/settings/MainSettings.java       | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/settings/MainSettings.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/settings/MainSettings.java
index 5103c95468..d54e5cd46b 100644
--- a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/settings/MainSettings.java
+++ b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/settings/MainSettings.java
@@ -557,11 +557,14 @@ public class MainSettings extends ChromeBaseSettingsFragment
             promoCardPreference.updatePreferences();
         }
 
-        if (shouldShowSignInPref(getProfile())) {
-            addPreferenceIfAbsent(PREF_SIGN_IN);
-        } else {
-            removePreferenceIfPresent(PREF_SIGN_IN);
-        }
+        // De-Googled build: remove the whole "You and Google" section. Sign-in
+        // does not work here (no Google API keys) and Sync is not part of this
+        // build, so the row and the Google services page only lead to features
+        // that cannot function. The section header is removed too, otherwise an
+        // empty heading is left behind.
+        removePreferenceIfPresent(PREF_SIGN_IN);
+        removePreferenceIfPresent(PREF_GOOGLE_SERVICES);
+        removePreferenceIfPresent(PREF_ACCOUNT_AND_GOOGLE_SERVICES_SECTION);
 
         updateSearchEnginePreference();
         updateAutofillPreferences();
